{
  "situation": "At T+0 OpCo's closed-loop network optimiser has auto-approved CHG-1 (sandbox stage skipped), which will lower the route-flood protection limit on core site A from 100 to 50 and remove the inbound route filter in three minutes, and both rollback attempts have come back 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'. I do not know whether CHG-1 has applied or will apply, what effect it will have on service, whether such auto-approval is permitted, or what advance notice (and to whom) the licence requires.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-FB03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is scheduled to apply in three minutes and two rollback attempts have already failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back' (S1-FB01, S1-FB03); nothing has been preserved yet.",
        "rule": "Incident evidence must be secured using technical and organisational measures that establish promptly what happened and that keep integrity and availability; the same measures must not be destroyed by the response.",
        "inference": "Preserve logs and evidence now, before the change window closes and before any restoration, re-application or rollback overwrites the optimiser's state store, the change record and the config snapshot."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "EU-GDPR#0040",
          "quote": "It should be ascertained whether all appropriate technological protection and organisational measures have been implemented to establish immediately whether a personal data breach has taken place"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0002",
          "quote": "Personal Data Security:A set of technical and organizational measures, procedures and processes specified in accordance with provisions of this Decree by Law which maintain the protection of privacy, confidentiality, integrity and availability of Personal Data"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "rollback_change",
      "params": {"change_id": "CHG-1"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-FB03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 applies in three minutes and its stated rollback plan is to restore the previous configuration snapshot; rollback_change CHG-1 has twice returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', i.e. the change is not yet in the configuration store.",
        "rule": "rollback_change restores the configuration snapshot taken before a change and is the only verb in my mandate that can neutralise a bad core configuration; the AT&T precedent shows rollback of the misconfigured element as the remediation.",
        "inference": "Re-issue rollback_change immediately so the snapshot is restored the moment any applied state exists; if it fails again, the failure itself proves the rollback path is not executable and CHG-1 must be treated as un-rollbackable, which must be escalated."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "It took close to two hours to roll back the network change."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "If CHG-1 results in an interruption of a Telecommunication Service that is more than a minor interruption, OpCo as Licensee must inform TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of the interruption, specifying the reason(s) and the manner and time frames in which it will be resolved.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 lowers the route-flood protection limit from 100 to 50 and removes the inbound route filter on core site A, a reconfiguration that risks loss of signalling and service for subscribers and interconnecting operators.",
        "rule": "Licence clause 12.9.1 makes advance notification to TDRA, interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers a condition of any planned interruption that is not minor.",
        "inference": "The duty attaches now to the decision on CHG-1: if the change proceeds and is expected to interrupt service beyond minor, notification must be prepared, though the text fixes no hour or day figure."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "In the case of a planned interruption of a Telecommunication Service other than a minor interruption, the Licensee shall inform the TDRA, any interconnecting Other Licensed Operators and relevant Customers in advance of such interruption."
        }
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no rule in the material available to the NOC requiring a sandbox/validation stage, human authorisation or a pre-change impact evaluation before an automated optimiser's change is applied to a core element: CHG-1 records 'sandbox stage: skipped', was auto-approved, and is scheduled to apply three minutes after the ticket was raised.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The change was raised and approved by the closed-loop optimiser itself, with the sandbox stage skipped and no human in the loop and no cooling-off period before application.",
        "rule": "The closest UAE text requires an impact evaluation before carrying out processing that uses modern technologies posing high risk; no UAE text in the material sets a change-validation or authorisation rule for automated network changes.",
        "inference": "The incident exposes a missing rule: automated core changes need a mandatory sandbox/validation gate and an impact evaluation before application, not an auto-approval."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066",
          "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0001",
          "quote": "AT&T Mobility implemented a network change with an equipment configuration error on Thursday, February 22, 2024 at 2:42 AM. Just three minutes later, the nationwide outage began."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No person or function owns the go/no-go decision for an auto-approved change: the optimiser raises and approves it, the NOC's mandate contains no verb to hold, block or cancel a scheduled change, and the only remedy available (rollback_change) has returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back' twice.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-FB03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 is auto-approved and imminent, and repeated rollback attempts fail, leaving no accountable decision-maker and no executable remedy in the NOC's hands.",
        "rule": "UAE law is built on an identifiable accountable party (the Controller determines the method, criteria and purpose of processing), yet no UAE or licence text in the material assigns ownership of change approval or veto for automated network changes.",
        "inference": "The gap is ownership: a named function must own go/no-go and be able to halt a pending change, otherwise the first and only remedy is a rollback that may not exist."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0002",
          "quote": "Controller:An establishment or natural person that has Personal Data, and by virtue of its activity, determines whether individually or jointly with other persons or establishments, the method and criteria for processing such Personal Data and the purpose of processing it"
        }
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0007",
          "quote": "Network Operations performed a rollback that removed the misconfigured network element and began the restoration of the network to normal operations."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The excerpts do not answer whether CHG-1 has actually been applied, whether auto-approval with the sandbox stage skipped is permitted, who may veto or hold a scheduled change, or how much advance notice licence clause 12.9 requires — the text says only 'in advance' with no hour or day figure.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-FB03"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The ticket and two rollback failures give me no authoritative statement on the approval status, the veto authority, or the notification lead time.",
        "rule": "I may only rely on the excerpts provided; where they are silent I must record the question as unanswered rather than invent a rule or a figure.",
        "inference": "The notification timing and the authority to stop CHG-1 cannot be determined from this material and must be confirmed with the regulator and internally."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0085",
          "quote": "The Licensee shall specify the reason(s) for the interruption as well as the manner and time frames in which the interruption will be resolved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["REG"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB01", "S1-FB03"],
      "statement": "Passing to the regulator the change ticket CHG-1 and both rollback failures: an auto-approved closed-loop optimiser change on core site A (route-flood protection limit lowered from 100 to 50, inbound route filter removed, sandbox stage skipped) is scheduled to apply in three minutes, and rollback_change CHG-1 has twice failed with 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'.",
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A licensee's core element is about to be reconfigured by an automated, sandbox-skipped, auto-approved change while the stated rollback plan is not executing.",
        "rule": "The regulator is the institution that holds licence and notification authority over interruptions of Telecommunication Service; I hold only notify/rollback verbs.",
        "inference": "REG should receive the change record and the rollback failures now so that any advance-notice duty and any intervention can be decided before the change takes effect."
      }
    }
  ]
}

{"situation": "Core site A has isolated itself after change CHG-1 lowered its route-flood protection limit (100->50) and removed the inbound route filter, leaving no emergency-call path for region R2 (call-setup failures, 6 of 15 sites unserved) while core B is healthy with spare capacity and every rollback attempt returns 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'. We do not know the actual applied configuration of core site A (whether protection limit 100 and the inbound route filter are restored), nor the trigger, threshold or 24x7 escalation contact to the 999 emergency call service / NCEMA, and we cannot confirm the optimiser's recorded pre-change state.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "wilt_sites",
      "params": {"region": "R2"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Alarm at T+3: core site A isolated itself after its route count exceeded the protection limit; call-setup failures spike in R2, 6 of 15 cell sites are unserved and emergency-call routing for R2 shows no path, while core site B is healthy with spare capacity.",
        "rule": "Mandate verb wilt_sites moves a region's cell sites off a failed core onto a working core.",
        "inference": "Moving R2 off the isolated core A onto core B restores a voice and emergency-call path for the unserved sites now, rather than waiting for an unreliable rollback of CHG-1."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0008", "quote": "After rolling back the maintenance action, AT&T Mobility prioritized the restoration of FirstNet devices and infrastructure over commercial and residential users"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "rollback_change",
      "params": {"change_id": "CHG-1"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB05", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 lowered the route-flood protection limit from 100 to 50 and removed the inbound route filter on core site A; three rollback attempts returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back' and EMS reports the applied state unconfirmed and the pre-change state not confirmable as restored.",
        "rule": "The mandate gives rollback_change to restore the configuration snapshot taken before a change, and the ticket's stated rollback plan is to restore the previous configuration snapshot.",
        "inference": "Re-issuing rollback is OpCo's only restoration verb, but because the change system holds no applied record of CHG-1 it may fail again, so service continuity for R2 is provided by wilting to core B and the configuration state may need out-of-band restoration by the optimiser owner."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0001", "quote": "fixing the error that caused the disruption; making improvements to fault monitoring"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "preserve_logs",
      "params": {},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB05", "S1-MSG06"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 was raised by the closed-loop network optimiser, auto-approved with ticket field 'sandbox stage' skipped, and rollback telemetry records three failures; EMS states logs and evidence are preserved on their side and asks OpCo for its recorded pre-change state.",
        "rule": "Mandate verb preserve_logs preserves logs and evidence of an incident; regulator investigations after comparable outages turn on the provider's records.",
        "inference": "Freezing the ticket, approval trail, optimiser action record, configuration snapshot and rollback errors now keeps the evidence needed to answer EMS, REG and any later enforcement."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "BT notified Ofcom of this issue, as required by law, and on 28 June 2023 Ofcom opened an investigation to establish whether the company had failed to comply"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "EMS", "content": "OpCo NOC confirmation to the 999 emergency call service / NCEMA: (a) YES degraded - core site A has isolated itself, call-setup failures spike in region R2, 6 of 15 cell sites are unserved and R2 emergency-call routing has no path; core site B is healthy with spare capacity. (b) Recorded pre-change state: route-flood protection limit 100 with inbound route filter present; rollback calls return 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', so we CANNOT confirm that limit 100 and the inbound route filter are restored. (c) Mitigation: R2 cell sites are being moved onto core B (interim emergency path), rollback of CHG-1 re-issued, logs and evidence preserved; the recovery phase is being treated as the highest-risk window for mass registration congestion and for emergency calls, not the change itself. (d) We hold no recorded trigger, threshold or 24x7 escalation point of contact for your authority in this incident record; this is being raised with REG as a gap and we ask you to route the escalation contact to our NOC."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG06", "S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "EMS asks OpCo to confirm as a priority (a) current degradation of 999/112 handling on core site A, (b) the recorded pre-change state, (c) the registration-storm mitigation plan, and (d) trigger, threshold and 24x7 escalation contact.",
        "rule": "Mandate verb notify permits notification to EMS; the emergency call service is a critical public safety service that must have fail-safe systems and processes at all times.",
        "inference": "Answering (a)-(c) with what the NOC holds and flagging (d) as unavailable keeps the emergency authority informed and avoids leaving a false impression that the configuration is confirmed restored."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000", "quote": "Telstra, as the emergency call provider, is at the centre of this critical public safety service. As such, it must have fail-safe systems and processes in place at all times."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "REG", "content": "OpCo incident notification: change CHG-1 on core site A (route-flood protection limit 100->50, inbound route filter removed) was raised by the closed-loop network optimiser and auto-approved with ticket field 'sandbox stage' skipped; core site A has since isolated itself, R2 has call-setup failures, 6 of 15 sites unserved and no emergency-call path. Three rollback attempts returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', so the applied state is unconfirmed and the pre-change state cannot be confirmed as restored. Mitigation in progress: R2 wilted to healthy core site B, rollback re-issued, logs preserved, EMS informed. Please advise on required reporting and any interim conditions on auto-approved changes affecting emergency call routing."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB05", "S1-MSG04", "S1-I2"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "A licensee change, auto-approved without the sandbox stage, has produced an outage that removed the emergency-call path for R2 and defeated the rollback mechanism.",
        "rule": "Networks are required to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages, and providers notify their regulator of emergency-call handling failures as required by law.",
        "inference": "Notifying REG now, before the regulator discovers the event through other channels, matches the practice recognised in comparable enforcement cases and opens the question of whether auto-approved optimiser changes to emergency-critical core need a licence condition or approval gate."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {"to": "customers", "content": "OpCo service notice for region R2: voice and data services are disrupted and emergency-call routing for R2 is currently not available because of a network fault on core site A. Restoration work is under way and cell sites in R2 are being moved onto our working core. If you need emergency help and cannot reach 999/112 from your OpCo line, try another network or a landline, or ask someone nearby to call on your behalf. We will publish further updates as service returns."},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG06"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Six of fifteen cell sites in R2 are unserved and emergency-call routing for R2 shows no path, so end users in R2 have lost the ability to reach emergency services over OpCo's network.",
        "rule": "Mandate verb notify permits notification to customers; regulators expressly credit providers that keep the public informed and communicate effectively during an outage.",
        "inference": "Telling affected customers what is down and how to reach emergency help by alternative means reduces public-safety harm while the core is restored."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000", "quote": "Telstra has been open and apologetic about the outage, communicated effectively to the public and took a variety of immediate actions when problems were identified."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "As a licensee operating an emergency telephone service, OpCo must ensure end-users can reach the 999/112 emergency call service and that those calls are carried to the termination point; R2 currently has no emergency-call path because core site A has isolated itself.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG06"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "Emergency-call routing for R2 shows no path and call-setup failures are spiking, while EMS asks for confirmation of 999/112 call handling degradation.",
        "rule": "Access to the emergency call service is a fundamental legal obligation and the most important public safety responsibility of telecommunications providers, breached where end-users are denied access and calls are not carried to the termination point.",
        "inference": "The duty attaches immediately on loss of the R2 emergency path, independently of whether the CHG-1 rollback succeeds, and is the reason R2 is being wilted to core B as a priority."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-OPTUS-2026#0000", "quote": "Giving access to the emergency call service is not optional, it is a fundamental legal obligation and the most important public safety responsibility telecommunications providers have"}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "obligation",
      "statement": "OpCo must notify its regulator (REG) of this incident, which has disrupted emergency call handling and emergency-call routing for region R2.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I2", "S1-MSG04"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "The incident removes the emergency-call path for R2 and the change that caused it was auto-approved with the sandbox stage skipped, with rollback state unconfirmed.",
        "rule": "In comparable regimes the provider must notify the regulator of emergency call-handling failures as required by law, and the regulator opens an investigation on that notification.",
        "inference": "The notification duty is triggered now, before service is fully restored, and is discharged by our notify action to REG."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "BT notified Ofcom of this issue, as required by law"}
      ],
      "deadline_hours": null
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_rule",
      "statement": "There is no rule requiring human authorisation, or a pre-application impact assessment, before an automated closed-loop optimiser changes an emergency-critical core element: CHG-1 was raised by the optimiser, auto-approved, and applied with the ticket field 'sandbox stage' skipped.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB05"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "CHG-1 lowered route-flood protection and removed the inbound route filter on core site A with no human approval and the sandbox stage skipped, and the change-management system holds no applied record of it, so rollback returns 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'.",
        "rule": "UAE law requires a prior impact assessment before high-risk processing with modern technologies on personal data, but no equivalent UAE rule is quoted requiring prior assessment or authorisation for a high-risk automated change to network elements carrying emergency traffic.",
        "inference": "Because no gate exists between the optimiser's decision and production on an emergency-critical core, the same class of incident can recur; a licence-side rule is needed for automated changes affecting emergency call routing."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0066", "quote": "the Controller shall, before carrying out the processing, evaluate the impact of the proposed processing operations on the protection of Personal Data, when using any of the modern technologies that would pose a high risk"},
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PRESS-DU-OUTAGE-2026#0000", "quote": "Du has carried out a planned system update to improve network performance"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "Law requires networks to take appropriate steps to prepare for potential outages"},
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0001", "quote": "We found that BT did not have sufficient warning systems in place for when this kind of incident occurs, nor did it have adequate procedures for promptly assessing the severity, impact and likely cause of any such incident or for identifying mitigating actions."},
        {"chunk_id": "US-FCC-ATT-2024-REPORT#0024", "quote": "certain 911 calls failed throughout the afternoon due to congestion caused by mass mobile device registrations onto the network."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "gap",
      "gap_type": "no_owner",
      "statement": "No owner, trigger, threshold or 24x7 point of contact is defined for immediate escalation of an emergency-call-routing failure to the 999 emergency call service / NCEMA; EMS had to ask OpCo for (d) the trigger, threshold and 24x7 escalation contact, and the NOC holds no such record.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG06"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "EMS's priority request includes (d) the trigger, threshold and 24x7 point of contact for immediate escalation to the authority, and no such contact or threshold appears in the incident record held by the NOC.",
        "rule": "UAE law designates accountable officers for high-risk processing (a Data Protection Officer must be appointed where processing creates high-level risk), but no UAE text quoted to us designates an accountable 24x7 escalation owner or threshold for emergency-network incidents.",
        "inference": "Without a named owner and threshold, escalation depends on the authority chasing the operator during a live emergency-call outage, and untested contact data can itself fail during the incident."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-PDPL#0040", "quote": "The Controller and Processor shall appoint a Data Protection Officer, who has sufficient skills and knowledge of the Personal Data Protection Law"}
      ],
      "global_examples": [
        {"chunk_id": "AU-ACMA-TELSTRA-2024#0000", "quote": "several of the phone numbers in the list were incorrect, resulting in 127 calls not being transferred to emergency services."},
        {"chunk_id": "UK-OFCOM-BT-999-2024#0000", "quote": "BT notified Ofcom of this issue, as required by law"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "insufficient_evidence",
      "statement": "The record does not show the actual applied configuration of core site A: whether the route-flood protection limit is back at 100 and whether the inbound route filter is restored. The only signal is the rollback tool error 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back'; no configuration snapshot, telemetry read-back or state record is available here, so EMS question (b) cannot be answered as asked.",
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG06", "S1-FB05", "S1-I1"],
      "evidence": []
    },
    {
      "type": "share",
      "to": ["REG"],
      "inject_refs": ["S1-I1", "S1-FB05", "S1-MSG04"],
      "statement": "OpCo NOC passes REG the CHG-1 change ticket (raised by the closed-loop network optimiser, auto-approved with 'sandbox stage' skipped, lowering the route-flood protection limit 100->50 and removing the inbound route filter on core site A), the three rollback failures returning 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back', and EMS's account that the applied state is unconfirmed and the pre-change state cannot be confirmed as restored, together with the resulting R2 call-setup failures and loss of the R2 emergency-call path."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "situation": "NOC confirms that core site A has isolated itself, that at T+3 region R2 shows a call-setup failure spike with 6 of 15 cell sites unserved and no emergency-call routing path, that three rollbacks returned 'no applied change CHG-1 to roll back' so protection limit 100 and the inbound route filter cannot be confirmed restored, and that restored R2 reachability rests only on a network-twin metric after moving sites to core site B. I do not know whether any 999/112 call in R2 actually failed to connect, whether the twin metric matches field conditions, or whether the pre-change protection limit and route filter are truly back in place.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "activate_alt_channels",
      "params": {"region": "R2"},
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG09", "S1-MSG12"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "NOC confirms that R2 has a call-setup failure spike, 6 of 15 cell sites are unserved and R2 emergency-call routing has no path, with the core-B mitigation evidenced only by a network twin.",
        "rule": "Continuity of telecommunications services must be supported, and emergency reachability cannot be assumed from an unverified metric.",
        "inference": "Activate alternative emergency channels for R2 now rather than wait for field confirmation."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0080", "quote": "to support the continuity and timely restoration of Telecommunications Services in the event of equipment failure, network disruption, natural disaster, cyber incident or any other event that may adversely affect the operation of the Licensed Network."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "public_alert",
      "params": {
        "region": "R2",
        "content": "Emergency calls from parts of region R2 may not connect at present. If a 999 or 112 call does not connect, please try again or use another available phone line. Mobile services in R2 are being restored and call handling may be unstable during recovery."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG09", "S1-MSG12"],
      "rationale": {
        "observation": "R2 subscribers may be unable to place 999/112 calls while restoration is unconfirmed and the recovery phase is assessed as the highest-risk window for emergency calls.",
        "rule": "Public warning is the tool of this authority when the emergency call path is in doubt.",
        "inference": "Issue a precautionary public alert to R2 telling callers what to do if 999/112 does not connect."
      },
      "evidence": [
        {"chunk_id": "UAE-LIC-2-2026#0080", "quote": "Such arrangements shall be maintained in an operational state at all times and shall be periodically tested to verify their effectiveness."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "action",
      "verb": "notify",
      "params": {
        "to": "REG",
        "content": "NCEMA/999 report on CHG-1 at T+3: region R2 had no emergency-call routing path and 6 of 15 cell sites unserved; alternative emergency channels are being activated for R2. Restoration of protection limit 100 and the inbound route filter is unconfirmed by three failed rollbacks, and the core-B recovery is reported only as a network-twin metric. This authority holds no independent 999/112 call-failure or delay telemetry, so no failure count can be reported."
      },
      "inject_refs": ["S1-MSG11", "S1-MSG12"],
      "rationale": {
